{"id":"u-91dc1e65-eb3f-4592-bbe4-77dc8497bd3e","src":"community","title":"Juggernaut General Peaking","author":"Punith G.","url":"https://www.boostcamp.app/users/yaVKB1-juggernaut-general-peaking","desc":"This program is directly inspired by and based on the peaking principles taught by Chad Wesley Smith of Juggernaut Training Systems. Before running this program, you are strongly encouraged to watch Chad’s original video explaining the why behind the structure, loading, and tapering:\n\n👉 https://youtu.be/gETcVcujE-I\n\nThis program is a true peaking block for powerlifting, built to help lifters express the highest possible strength at the right time, whether that’s on a competition platform or across split max days in the gym.\n\nIt is directly modeled on the exact example peaking framework taught by Chad Wesley Smith of Juggernaut Training Systems, translating Juggernaut’s proven principles into a clear, structured, and reusable format.\n\nThe program prioritizes:\n\nHigh-intensity, low-volume training (85%+)\n\nCompetition-specific lifts and technique\n\nNeural force production and skill refinement\n\nIntentional fatigue decay through tapering\n\nStrategic exposure to heavy singles without overreaching\n\nRather than chasing gym PRs week after week, the goal is to accumulate fitness early, then remove fatigue so peak performance occurs when it matters most. Heavy squat and deadlift stress are intelligently alternated, bench press frequency is managed for faster recovery, and technique-focused sessions preserve motor patterns while accelerating recovery.\n\nTwo peak outcomes are supported:\n\nCompetition-style peak, where squat, bench, and deadlift are performed on the same day\n\nNon-competition (split) peak, where each lift is maxed on separate days for optimal recovery and expression\n\nThis is not a beginner program. It is designed for intermediate to advanced lifters who understand percentages, RPE, and the purpose of peaking.\n\nIf you’ve ever wondered how elite lifters outperform their gym numbers on meet day, this is the structure that makes that possible.","level":["Intermediate","Advanced","Beginner"],"goals":["Strength"],"equipment":["Full Gym"],"minutes":90,"joins":10,"rate":0,"rateCount":1,"updated":"2026-11-03T00:25:18.591Z","variations":[{"name":"default","days":["Day 1","Day 2","Day 3","Day 4"],"weeks":[[{"ex":[{"n":"Squat (Barbell)","sets":[{"r":2,"pct":92.5}],"note":"COMPETITION SQUAT!!!\nIntensity: 92.5-95%"},{"n":"Squat (Barbell)","sets":[{"r":3,"pct":82.5,"x":3}],"note":"COMPETITION SQUAT!!!"},{"n":"Deadlift (Barbell)","sets":[{"lo":1,"hi":2,"pct":40,"x":5}],"note":"TECHNIQUE DEADLIFT!!!\nIntensity: 40-60%\nSets: 5-8"}]},{"ex":[{"n":"Bench Press (Barbell)","sets":[{"r":1,"rpe":8.5}],"note":"COMPETITION BENCH!!!"},{"n":"Bench Press (Barbell)","sets":[{"r":3,"pct":85,"x":4}],"note":"COMPETITION BENCH!!!\nIntensity: 85-90%"}]},{"ex":[{"n":"Deadlift (Barbell)","sets":[{"r":2,"pct":85,"x":4}],"note":"COMPETITION DEADLIFT!!!\nIntensity: 85-90%\nRPE: 7-8"},{"n":"High Bar Squat (Barbell)","sets":[{"r":4,"pct":80,"x":3}]}]},{"ex":[{"n":"Bench Press (Close Grip)","sets":[{"r":5,"pct":77.5,"x":2}],"note":"Intensity: 77.5-82.5%"},{"n":"Larsen Press (Barbell)","sets":[{"r":5,"pct":77.5,"x":2}],"note":"Intensity: 77.5-82.5%"}]}],[{"ex":[{"n":"Squat (Barbell)","sets":[{"lo":2,"hi":3,"pct":85,"x":4}],"note":"COMPETITION SQUAT!!!\nSets: 4-5"},{"n":"Deadlift (Barbell)","sets":[{"lo":1,"hi":2,"pct":40,"x":5}],"note":"TECHNIQUE DEADLIFT!!!\nIntensity: 40-60%\nSets: 5-8"}]},{"ex":[{"n":"Bench Press (Barbell)","sets":[{"r":1,"rpe":9}],"note":"COMPETITION BENCH!!!"},{"n":"Bench Press (Barbell)","sets":[{"r":2,"pct":87,"x":3}],"note":"COMPETITION BENCH!!!\nIntensity: 87-92%"}]},{"ex":[{"n":"Deadlift (Barbell)","sets":[{"r":1,"rpe":9,"rpeHi":9.5}],"note":"COMPETITION DEADLIFT!!!"},{"n":"Deadlift (Barbell)","sets":[{"lo":1,"hi":2,"x":2}],"note":"COMPETITION DEADLIFT!!!\nIntensity: 80-90% of 1RM done just before this\nSets: 2-3"}